// Data: M57-Patents (Digital Corpora, CC0). See tests/THIRD-PARTY.md.
// Constructed: the M57 SSLv3 handshake from `tls-sslv3-certificate` with the server address added as SNI, since all IP-literal SNIs in M57 are SSLv2 attempts without a handshake. The TLS object keeps the SNI, which does not become the server host name.
from_file env("TENZIR_INPUT") {
  read_suricata
}
suricata::ocsf::normalize
this = ocsf_cast(ocsf_derive(this))
drop_null_fields
